<?xpacket begin="ï»¿" id="W5M0MpCehiHzreSzNTczkc9d"?>
<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">I had a dream (I got everything I wanted)</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;Adora had been asked out a couple times just this year alone and the girls had all been smart, beautiful, and on paper even good for her.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Starla still stuck out in her mind. For all intents and purposes, she was perfect for her. They were both English majors. She got Adoraâ€™s dorky sense of humor. She was a good listener. She went out of her way to take care of Adora making sure she didnâ€™t stress herself out to the point of passing out when she decided to take on almost a double course load sending her â€œtake a breakâ€ reminder texts most of the semester. They even went to the same fucking horse camp growing up even though they never met while there. There was just one problem.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;There was always just one problem.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Adora had been in love with Catra since one brown eye and one blue eye met her own in Kindergarten, offering her two broken crayons as she wailed long after Hope had dropped her off on the first day of school.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;or&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Adora has been in love with Catra their entire lives together. She was never going to tell her. Until she does.&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
